Sweep the [G#]streets I used to [Fm]own


{end_of_verse}
{start_of_verse: Interlude}
[C#] [D#add11] [G#] [Fm] x2


{end_of_verse}
{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
I used to [C#]roll the [D#add11]dice
Feel the [G#]fear in my enemy's [Fm]eyes
Listen as the [C#]crowd would [D#add11]sing:
"Now the [G#]old king is dead! Long [Fm]live the king!"
One minute I [C#]held the [D#add11]key
Next the [G#]walls were closed on [Fm]me
And I discovered that my [C#]castles [D#add11]stand
Upon [G#]pillars of salt and pill[Fm]ars of sand


{end_of_verse}
{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
I [C#]hear Jerusalem [D#add11]bells are ringing
[G#]Roman Cavalry [Fm]choirs are singing
[C#]Be my mirror, my [D#add11]sword and shield
My [G#]missionaries in a [Fm]foreign field
[C#]For some reason I [D#add11]can't explain
[G#]Once you'd gone there was [Fm]never
Never an [C#]honest [D#add11]word
And that was [Cm]when I ruled the [Fm]world


{end_of_chorus}
{start_of_verse: Interlude}
[C#] [D#add11] [G#] [Fm] x2


{end_of_verse}
{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
It was the wicked and [C#]wild [D#add11]wind
Blew down the [G#]doors to let me [Fm]in
Shattered windows and the [C#]sound of [D#add11]drums
People [G#]couldn't believe what [Fm]I'd become
Revolutio[C#]naries [D#add11]wait
For my [G#]head on a silver [Fm]plate
Just a puppet on a [C#]lonely [D#add11]string
Oh, [G#]who would ever want to be [Fm]king?


{end_of_verse}
{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
I [C#]hear Jerusalem [D#add11]bells are ringing
[G#]Roman Cavalry [Fm]choirs are singing
[C#]Be my mirror, my [D#add11]sword and shield
My [G#]missionaries in a [Fm]foreign field
[C#]For some reason I [D#add11]can't explain
I [G#]know Saint Peter won't [Fm]call my name
Never an [C#]honest [D#add11]word
But that was [Cm]when I ruled the [Fm]world


{end_of_chorus}
{start_of_verse: Interlude}
[C#] [Fm] x3
[D#add11] [D#add11]

Oh[C#]hhhh[D#add11]h       Oh[G#]hhhh[Fm]h
Oh[C#]hhhh[D#add11]h       Oh[G#]hhhh[Fm]h


{end_of_verse}
{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
