[C]Speaking words of [G]wisdom, let it [F]be[C/E][Dm7][C]
{end_of_verse}


{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
Let it [Am]be, let it [G]be, let it [F]be, let it [C]be
[C]Whisper words of [G]wisdom, let it [F]be[C/E][Dm7][C]
{end_of_chorus}


{start_of_verse: Strophe 2}
And [C]when the broken [G]hearted people, [Am]living i[Am/G]n the [Fmaj7]world ag[F6]ree
[C]There will be an a[G]nswer, let it b[F]e[C/E][Dm7][C]
For t[C]hough they may be par[G]ted, there is [Am]still a ch[Am/G]ance that th[Fmaj7]ey will s[F6]ee
[C]There will be an a[G]nswer, let it b[F]e[C/E][Dm7][C]
{end_of_verse}


{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
Let it b[Am]e, let it [G]be, let it [F]be, let it [C]be
[C]There will be an [G]answer, let it [F]be[C/E][Dm7][C]
Let it [Am]be, let it [G]be, let i[F]t be, let i[C]t be
[C]Whisper words of [G]wisdom, let it [F]be[C/E][Dm7][C]
{end_of_chorus}


{start_of_verse: Strophe 3}
And wh[C]en the night is cl[G]oudy,
There is [Am]still a light [Am/G]that sh[Fmaj7]ines on me[F6]
Shi[C]ne on till tom[G]orrow, let it b[F]e[C/E][Dm7][C]
I w[C]ake up to the [G]sound of music, [Am]Mother [Am/G]Mary [Fmaj7]comes to [F6]me
[C]Speaking words of [G]wisdom, let it [F]be[C/E][Dm7][C]
{end_of_verse}


{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
Let it [Am]be, let it [G]be, let it [F]be, let it [C]be
