songs.text:
{title: Hey Jude}
{artist: The Beatles}
{key: F}


{start_of_verse: Strophe 1}
Hey [F]Jude, don't make it [C]bad
Take [F/C]a   [C7]sad [C7sus4]song and [C7]make it [F]better
Re[Bb]member to let her into your [F]heart
and then you can [C]start to make it [F]better
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Strophe 2}
Hey [F]Jude, don't be a[C]fraid
You [F/C]were [C7]made [C7sus4]to  go [C7]out and [F]get her
The [Bb]minute you let her under your [F]skin
then you be[C]gin to make it [F]better[Fmaj7][F7]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
And anytime you feel the [Bb]pain, hey [Bb/A]Jude, re[Gm]frain
Don't [Bb/F]carry the [C/E]world u[C]pon your [F]shoulders[Fmaj7][F7]
For well you know that it's a [Bb]fool who [Bb/A]plays it [Gm]cool
by [Bb/F]making his [C/E]world a [C]little [F]colder
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Interlude}
[F]Na na na  [F7]na na   [C]na na  [C7]na naa[C][F][C7]
{end_of_bridge}


{start_of_verse: Strophe 3}
Hey [F]Jude, don't let me [C]down
You [F/C]have [C7]found [C7sus4]her, now [C7]go and [F]get her
Re[Bb]member to let her into you [F]heart
then you can [C]start to make it [F]better[Fmaj7][F7]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
So let it out and let it [Bb]in, hey [Bb/A]Jude, be[Gm]gin
You're [Bb/F]waiting for [C/E]someone [C]to per[F]form with[Fmaj7][F7]
And don't you know that it's just [Bb]you, hey [Bb/A]Jude, you'll [Gm]do
The [Bb/F]movement you [C/E]need is [C]on your [F]shoulders
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Interlude}
[F]Na na na  [F7]na na   [C]na na  [C7]na naa    [C]yea[F]h[C7]
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Strophe 4}
Hey [F]Jude, don't make it [C]bad
Take [F/C]a   [C7]sad [C7sus4]song and [C7]make it [F]better
Re[Bb]member to let her under your [F]skin
and then you'll [C]begin to make it [F]better, better, better, better, better, better, ahhhhhh!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
